selector_to_html = {"a[href=\"#pyskyfire.ducts.half_moon.HalfMoonSection.slit_boundary\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.ducts.half_moon.HalfMoonSection.slit_boundary\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">slit_boundary</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">size</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">aspect</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>The reserved slit alone, as a boundary piece in the section frame.</p><p>The same wall curve the section is drawn with, read only between the\nslit\u2019s own bounds. What comes back is the strip the cooling channels\nbreak out through, which is otherwise indistinguishable from the rest\nof the chamber-facing face.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"../volute_section/VoluteSection.html#pyskyfire.ducts.volute_section.VoluteSection\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.ducts.volute_section.VoluteSection\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.ducts.volute_section.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">VoluteSection</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">inlet_width</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">aspect_ratio</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">1.0</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">max_aspect_ratio</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Bases: <a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/library/abc.html#abc.ABC\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><code class=\"xref py py-obj docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">abc.ABC</span></code></a></p><p>A volute cross-section family with a fixed inlet slot width.</p><p>Subclasses define a shape parameterised by a positive <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">size</span></code> and an\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">aspect</span></code>. All methods accept a scalar or a one-dimensional array of\nsizes, and return matching arrays; <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">aspect</span></code> defaults to the family\u2019s own\n<code class=\"xref py py-attr docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">aspect_ratio</span></code> where it is not given.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#pyskyfire.ducts.half_moon.HalfMoonSection.exposed_wall\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.ducts.half_moon.HalfMoonSection.exposed_wall\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">exposed_wall</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">size</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">aspect</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Arc of wall left clear between the two fillets [m].</p><p>Equal to <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">size</span></code>: the fillets are tangent to the chord at the ends of\nthe exposed arc, so they begin where it ends rather than eating into\nit. Reported so that a design can be checked against the room the\nchannel breakout actually needs.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#pyskyfire.ducts.half_moon.HalfMoonSection.meridional_frame\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.ducts.half_moon.HalfMoonSection.meridional_frame\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">meridional_frame</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">size</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">aspect</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Where each section sits on the wall, as <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">(axial,</span> <span class=\"pre\">radial,</span> <span class=\"pre\">tilt)</span></code>.</p><p>A manifold\u2019s section slides along the wall as the area law resizes it,\nand leans with whatever the wall is doing there, so it carries its own\nplacement rather than taking one from the passage. <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">tilt</span></code> is the angle\nof the section\u2019s outward direction from radial, positive toward <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">+x</span></code>,\nwhich is what a sweep needs to lay the section plane down correctly.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#pyskyfire.ducts.half_moon.HalfMoonSection\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.ducts.half_moon.HalfMoonSection\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.ducts.half_moon.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">HalfMoonSection</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">profile</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">slit_height</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">fillet_radius</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"keyword-only-separator o\"><abbr title=\"Keyword-only parameters separator (PEP 3102)\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></abbr></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">slit_placement</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">0.5</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">exposure_placement</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">0.5</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">aspect_ratio</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">1.0</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">max_aspect_ratio</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Bases: <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../volute_section/VoluteSection.html#pyskyfire.ducts.volute_section.VoluteSection\" title=\"pyskyfire.ducts.volute_section.VoluteSection\"><code class=\"xref py py-obj docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.ducts.volute_section.VoluteSection</span></code></a></p><p>A manifold section: chamber wall inboard, half-ellipse outboard.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#pyskyfire.ducts.half_moon.HalfMoonSection.slit\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.ducts.half_moon.HalfMoonSection.slit\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">property</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">slit</span></span></dt><dd><p>Arc-length bounds of the reserved slit [m], about the anchor.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#pyskyfire.ducts.half_moon.HalfMoonSection._tangency\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.ducts.half_moon.HalfMoonSection._tangency\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">_tangency</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">chord</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">aspects</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Ellipse parameter where each fillet touches it.</p><p>The fillet centres sit one radius inboard of the chord at each of its\nends, so requiring the ellipse to be tangent to both \u2013 and centred on\nthe chord \u2013 leaves a single equation. It is monotone on <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">(0,</span> <span class=\"pre\">pi/2)</span></code>,\nrunning to plus infinity as the parameter approaches the chord and to\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">-fillet_radius</span></code> at the outboard extreme, so the bracket is fixed.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#pyskyfire-ducts-half-moon-halfmoonsection\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">pyskyfire.ducts.half_moon.HalfMoonSection<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#pyskyfire-ducts-half-moon-halfmoonsection\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1>", "a[href=\"#pyskyfire.ducts.half_moon.HalfMoonSection.margin_boundaries\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.ducts.half_moon.HalfMoonSection.margin_boundaries\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">margin_boundaries</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">size</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">aspect</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>The chamber-facing wall either side of the slit, as boundary pieces.</p><p>Returned in the order the face is traversed, so the two of them and\n<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#pyskyfire.ducts.half_moon.HalfMoonSection.slit_boundary\" title=\"pyskyfire.ducts.half_moon.HalfMoonSection.slit_boundary\"><code class=\"xref py py-meth docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">slit_boundary()</span></code></a> between them tile it exactly. That matters for\ndrawing: the slit is where channels break out and the rest of the face\nis metal against the chamber, and the two want telling apart without\nlaying one surface on top of the other.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#pyskyfire.ducts.half_moon.HalfMoonSection.maximum_size\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.ducts.half_moon.HalfMoonSection.maximum_size\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">property</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">maximum_size</span></span><span class=\"property\"><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">float</span></a></span></dt><dd><p>The most wall there is to spread onto, given where the slit sits.</p><p>The window opens either side of the fixed slit in the fixed ratio, so\nwhichever side runs out of wall first is what caps the section.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#pyskyfire.ducts.half_moon.HalfMoonSection.boundary\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.ducts.half_moon.HalfMoonSection.boundary\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">boundary</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">size</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">aspect</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Counterclockwise boundary pieces for each size and aspect.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#pyskyfire.ducts.half_moon.HalfMoonSection._frame\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.ducts.half_moon.HalfMoonSection._frame\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">_frame</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">size</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Chord frame of the exposed wall: origin, axes, and chord length.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#pyskyfire.ducts.half_moon.HalfMoonSection._layout\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.ducts.half_moon.HalfMoonSection._layout\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">_layout</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">size</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">aspect</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Resolve the chord frame, the ellipse, and both fillet arcs.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#pyskyfire.ducts.half_moon.HalfMoonSection.dome\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.ducts.half_moon.HalfMoonSection.dome\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">dome</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">size</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">aspect</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>The outboard dome, as <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">(depth,</span> <span class=\"pre\">half_width,</span> <span class=\"pre\">arc_limit)</span></code>.</p><p>The depth is how far the section reaches out along the normal from its\nchord and the half-width is the ellipse axis across it, both semi-axes\nof the ellipse the section is built on. The arc limit is the ellipse\nparameter the fillets take over at: only within it is the ellipse\npassage boundary, so it is what bounds where a port may leave through.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#pyskyfire.ducts.half_moon.HalfMoonSection.window\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.ducts.half_moon.HalfMoonSection.window\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">window</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">size</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Arc-length bounds of the exposed wall at each size [m].</p><p>The slit stays put and the spare wall divides about it in the fixed\nratio, so the window closes onto the slit as <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">size</span></code> reaches\n<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#pyskyfire.ducts.half_moon.HalfMoonSection.minimum_size\" title=\"pyskyfire.ducts.half_moon.HalfMoonSection.minimum_size\"><code class=\"xref py py-attr docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">minimum_size</span></code></a>.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#pyskyfire.ducts.half_moon.HalfMoonSection.minimum_size\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.ducts.half_moon.HalfMoonSection.minimum_size\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">property</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">minimum_size</span></span><span class=\"property\"><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">float</span></a></span></dt><dd><p>The slit itself, where the exposed wall has nothing left to give.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#pyskyfire.ducts.half_moon.HalfMoonSection.fan_origin\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.ducts.half_moon.HalfMoonSection.fan_origin\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">fan_origin</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">size</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">aspect</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>A point on the centreline that sees the whole boundary.</p><p>Outboard of the wall\u2019s own bulge, since a wall curving into the cavity\nwould otherwise hide part of itself from a point on the chord.</p></dd>"}
skip_classes = ["headerlink", "sd-stretched-link"]

window.onload = function () {
    for (const [select, tip_html] of Object.entries(selector_to_html)) {
        const links = document.querySelectorAll(` ${select}`);
        for (const link of links) {
            if (skip_classes.some(c => link.classList.contains(c))) {
                continue;
            }

            tippy(link, {
                content: tip_html,
                allowHTML: true,
                arrow: true,
                placement: 'auto-start', maxWidth: 600, interactive: false,
                onShow(instance) {MathJax.typesetPromise([instance.popper]).then(() => {});},
            });
        };
    };
    console.log("tippy tips loaded!");
};
